Patch against guybedford/workers-rs @ emscripten root Cargo.toml.

Two changes for a minimal QUIC build:
  1. Add a `[patch.crates-io]` entry routing `quinn-udp` to our patched copy
     (see quinn-udp-emscripten-fallback.patch).
  2. Drop the goose-only patches (arboard/fs2/sys-info/tree-sitter) and exclude the
     `emscripten-goose` example, so the workspace resolves without those submodules.

Adjust the `quinn-udp.path` to wherever you place the patched quinn-udp checkout.

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 9a6a1d9..1c0031e 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ members = [
 exclude = [
     "examples/coredump",
     "examples/axum",
+    "examples/emscripten-goose",
     "templates/*",
     "wasm-bindgen",
     "wasm-streams",
@@ -119,17 +120,19 @@ wasm-bindgen-macro-support = { version = "0.2.121", path = "./wasm-bindgen/crate
 wasm-bindgen-shared = { version = "0.2.121", path = "./wasm-bindgen/crates/shared" }
 wasm-bindgen-test = { version = "0.3.71", path = "./wasm-bindgen/crates/test" }
 web-sys = { version = "0.3.98", path = './wasm-bindgen/crates/web-sys' }
-arboard.path = "./arboard"
-fs2.path = "./fs2-rs"
 libc.path = "./libc"
 socket2.git = "https://github.com/rust-lang/socket2"
-sys-info.path = "./sys-info"
 ring.path = "./ring"
 tokio-macros.path = "./tokio/tokio-macros"
 tokio.path = "./tokio/tokio"
-# Emscripten has a full libc, so tree-sitter must not compile its libc-less
-# wasm shims (stdio/stdlib/...) — they duplicate `fwrite` et al. The local
-# `tree-sitter` submodule (emscripten branch, v0.26.9 base — matching goose's
-# req.) carries that build.rs fix.
-tree-sitter.path = "./tree-sitter/lib"
-tree-sitter-language.path = "./tree-sitter/crates/language"
+# quinn-udp is a hard dep of quinn but its unix path needs pktinfo cmsg structs
+# emscripten's libc lacks. We never use it (abstract socket), so route emscripten
+# to quinn-udp's fallback stub via this local patch.
+quinn-udp.path = "../quinn-udp"
+# --- goose-only patches (arboard/fs2/sys-info/tree-sitter) disabled for the
+# --- QUIC POC; emscripten-goose is excluded from the workspace above.
+# arboard.path = "./arboard"
+# fs2.path = "./fs2-rs"
+# sys-info.path = "./sys-info"
+# tree-sitter.path = "./tree-sitter/lib"
+# tree-sitter-language.path = "./tree-sitter/crates/language"
